1
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:01,950
Oh, it's a quarter to four,

2
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:04,520
and I have a production meeting at four.

3
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:06,900
I planned to take you for a ride in Central Park

4
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:08,840
in a horse and carriage.

5
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:10,010
Harry, I'd love to,

6
00:01:10,010 --> 00:01:12,420
but I have work to do.

7
00:01:12,420 --> 00:01:16,300
OK. We'll walk back to your office with you.

8
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,410
It's so nice out.

9
00:01:18,410 --> 00:01:20,900
I decided to forget about my accounting problems

10
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:24,530
and just enjoy this beautiful spring day.

11
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:26,370
Take the time, Susan.

12
00:01:26,370 --> 00:01:27,780
I know I should,

13
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:32,310
but ... well, there are too many things to do.

14
00:01:32,310 --> 00:01:33,370
I understand.

15
00:01:33,370 --> 00:01:35,840
I'll go for a ride with Michelle.

16
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:37,240
Right.

17
00:01:37,240 --> 00:01:41,620
Well, I had a really nice time.

18
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,850
So did I.

19
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:44,260
So did I.

20
00:01:44,260 --> 00:01:46,690
I'm sorry you can't come with us, Susan.

21
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:48,810
So am I.

22
00:01:48,810 --> 00:01:51,520
Bye-bye.

23
00:01:51,520 --> 00:01:59,790
Harry! Michelle! Can you wait till I make a phone call?

24
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:14,840
Sure.

25
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,810
Susan Stewart's office.

26
00:02:16,810 --> 00:02:18,280
Sam, this is Susan.

27
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:19,650
Hi. How was lunch?

28
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:21,260
Fine.

29
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:22,790
You're late.

30
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:25,420
The production department's waiting in the conference room.

31
00:02:25,420 --> 00:02:26,290
I know.

32
00:02:26,290 --> 00:02:28,110
Ask Paul Smith to fill in for me.

33
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:29,570
He knows everything about the production schedule,

34
00:02:29,570 --> 00:02:31,660
and he can answer any questions.

35
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,910
Right.

36
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:34,210
Don't tell any one,

37
00:02:34,210 --> 00:02:37,300
but I'm taking a little time to smell the flowers.

38
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:37,840
Good for you.

39
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:38,920
It'll be our secret.

40
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,200
But schedule another production meeting for tomorrow.

41
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:41,960
I'll be back

42
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:43,740
for my six o'clock appointment with Mr. Ozawa.

43
00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:44,430
OK, Susan.

44
00:02:44,430 --> 00:02:45,980
And have a nice afternoon.

45
00:02:45,980 --> 00:03:28,670
Thanks.

46
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:29,760
She likes you.

47
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:31,700
I know. I like her.

48
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:32,780
How'd you do it?

49
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,310
We had a talk.

50
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:35,570
About what?

51
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:37,240
Life.

52
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,750
And what did you decide?

53
00:03:38,750 --> 00:03:41,750
That's a secret ... between us women.
